;; amu's language ladder toward one typed source for kotoba-lang/browser
;; (ADR 0353, which decides ADR 0352).
;;
;; A floor is CLOSED only when its gate -- a `(deftest <gate>` in the floor's
;; repository (default kotoba-lang/amu) -- is on that repository's
;; origin/main. The superproject tick `scripts/amu-language-tick.cljk` reads
;; exactly that. The gate test must pin the admission AND the refusal the
;; floor keeps (ADR 0353 "What stays refused"). Order is the order the loop
;; takes them; an iteration may split or reorder a floor when measuring shows
;; the ladder was wrong, in the same commit, with the reason.
{:format :amu.language-ladder/v1
 :goal "kotoba-lang/browser as one typed source that amu compiles for the hosted engine and for x86_64-aiueos-kernel-v1 / aarch64-macos, without giving up safety, speed or code identity"
 :adr "0353"
 :floors
 [{:id :export-from-publicity :gate "export-derived-from-defn-publicity-test"
   :goal "a module's export vector is its public top-level definitions; defn- is private; an explicit :export still wins; the interface CID is computed from the public set"
   :amends "ADR 0005"}
  {:id :absence :gate "nil-field-is-absence-test"
   :goal "nil as a map-literal value makes the field [:option T] and absent; truthiness only on :bool and [:option T]; when / if-let / when-let / cond-> / some-> over an option desugar to option-match; strings and records are never truthy"
   :amends "ADR 0028"}
  ;; Split out of :absence (2026-09-25), because measuring showed it is not
  ;; the same change: the predicate primitives (`record-equal` was the one
  ;; measured) still answered the legacy 0/1 i64. Landed the same day at the
  ;; language surface, not through KIR: the six 0/1 operations (record-equal,
  ;; typed-map-equal, typed-set-equal, hetero-vector-equal, task-ready?,
  ;; object-cas-won) are elaborated to `(= op 1)` by kotoba-sema, so the KIR
  ;; operations and every backend are unchanged. Retiring the 0/1 KIR
  ;; answer itself is not needed for safety and is left to whoever measures a
  ;; cost in the extra compare.
  {:id :bool-predicates :gate "numbers-are-never-truthy-test"
   :goal "every predicate primitive answers :bool, not a 0/1 i64; an :i64 `if` / `when` / `if-let` test is refused by name; numbers are never truthy"
   :amends "ADR 0028"}
;; :row-records split in three (2026-09-25), because measuring showed three
  ;; changes in three places: inferring the row and monomorphizing the calls is
  ;; one kotoba-sema pass before parameter inference; the row OPERATIONS need
  ;; record types that are not declared schemas (assoc extends the row) and a
  ;; retirement of the keyword->i64 map that `{:a 5}` still lowers to; and a
  ;; specialization's CID derived from its generic's is amu's
  ;; definition-identity, which today hashes only monomorphic KIR (and
  ;; kotoba-hir's function schema refuses a key naming the generic).
  {:id :row-records :gate "row-polymorphic-record-inference-test"
   :goal "an unannotated parameter read as a record, or passed on to a row parameter, gets the row type {:k T | r} from those uses; its function exists only as its specializations, one per record type a call passes (monomorphized), each typed at that record; a non-record argument, a record lacking a field the row reads, an exported generic and a generic used as a value are refused by name"}
;; :row-operations split in two (2026-09-26), because measuring showed two
  ;; changes: the four operations are a type-directed elaboration in
  ;; kotoba-sema's `rewrite-record-projection` onto record-new / record-get /
  ;; record-assoc (nothing reaches KIR), while the rest is unification --
  ;; a map literal typed by the row it is passed to (today it lowers to the
  ;; keyword->i64 map before any row is known, and is refused as "map"),
  ;; `(if c m n)` joining two parameters, a loop helper made generic with its
  ;; function, and `(nth [(mk) (mk)] 1)` (refused "expected i64, got
  ;; [:ref :b/s]") -- each a change to inference, not to elaboration.
  {:id :row-operations :gate "row-operations-extend-and-shrink-test"
   :goal "assoc / dissoc / merge / select-keys are row operations whose results are record types: assoc extends, dissoc / select-keys shrink, merge assoc's a record's or a map literal's fields; a parameter a row operation uses is a row"}
  ;; :row-unification split in two (2026-09-26), because measuring showed two
  ;; changes in two places: a row argument, an if join and a loop helper are
  ;; all decided in kotoba-sema's row pass (`specialize-row-parameters`),
  ;; where the row is known; a vector literal of records and a let-bound map
  ;; literal are lowered by `desugar-expr` from their source alone, before
  ;; any type is inferred (`closed-vector-literal-type`,
  ;; `keyword-map-literal-record-fields`), and retiring the keyword->i64 map
  ;; changes the lowering -- and the definition CID -- of every all-i64
  ;; keyword literal, not only those a row receives.
  {:id :row-unification :gate "row-literal-join-and-loop-unification-test"
   :goal "a map literal passed to a row is that row's record; a parameter returned beside a row ((if c m n)) unifies into it, and two records at one join are refused by name; a loop over a row parameter is specialized with its function"}
  {:id :literal-typing :gate "record-vector-and-map-literal-retirement-test"
   :goal "a vector literal of records is an ordinary typed vector ((nth [(mk) (mk)] 1) is the record, today refused \"expected i64, got [:ref :b/s]\"); a keyword map literal is a record wherever it is written, including a let binding later passed to a row; the keyword->i64 map is retired"}
  {:id :specialization-identity :gate "specialization-cid-derived-from-generic-test"
   :goal "every row specialization's definition CID is derived from the generic definition's CID and its type arguments, so two modules specializing one generic at one record share a CID and ADR 0300's compile-once cache holds across them"}
  {:id :function-values :gate "function-value-in-record-test"
   :goal "a function type carries its effect row; a closure is a one-word ABI v8 handle that may be a record field or vector element; the ADR 0352 internal error on a stored closure is gone"}
  {:id :code-units :gate "string-code-unit-primitives-test"
   :goal "string-code-unit-count, string-code-unit-at and subs over code units are primitives; count of a string stays refused"}
  {:id :hiccup-node :gate "hiccup-literal-is-node-adt-test"
   :goal "Node = Text | Elem tag attrs [Node] | Frag [Node] over ABI v8 [:ref q]; a hiccup literal desugars to it; shape tests over hiccup become an exhaustive variant-match"}
  {:id :allocation-budget :gate "allocation-charged-to-fuel-test"
   :goal "every constructor debits the 64-bit fuel ledger; the ADT node/depth ceilings are the caller's budget, not the constants 64 / 12"
   :amends "osaho adt-node-limit / adt-depth-limit"}
  {:id :definition-admission :gate "admission-by-definition-graph-test"
   :goal "the 1 MiB bound moves from linked source bytes to per-definition size and closure count; cssom/layout.cljk (1,083,132 bytes) is admitted definition by definition"
   :amends "ADR 0005 linked-source bound"}
  {:id :native-handles :gate "native-record-vector-closure-boundary-test"
   :goal "kotoba-native qualifies record, vector and closure handles as loop-helper boundary types and retires map-new; record-assoc is qualified, and kotoba-verifier's record projection sees through a let operand (a row operation elaborates to (record-get T (let [..] (record-new T ..)) :f), refused today as runtime KIR record projection rejected, exit 65, hand-written too); the forms of every floor above compile for x86_64-aiueos-kernel-v1 and aarch64-macos (target refusals exit 65, not 70)"}
  {:id :browser-text-edit :gate "browser-text-edit-native-test"
   :goal "kotoba-lang/browser's browser.text-edit, migrated only mechanically (defn-, nil's meaning, a :kotoba interop branch), compiles for both native targets and its hosted tests pass on amu's output"}
  {:id :browser-input :gate "browser-input-native-test"
   :goal "browser.input the same"}
  {:id :browser-surface :gate "browser-surface-native-test"
   :goal "browser.surface with cssom.layout and kotoba.wasm.dom the same"}
  {:id :hosted-engine-switch :gate "browser-hosted-runs-amu-output-test" :repo "kotoba-lang/browser"
   :goal "kotoba-lang/browser's hosted engine runs amu's compiled output of its own source; the Clojure source is that source, not a second copy"}
  ;; The selfhost foundation (appended 2026-09-26, superproject
  ;; adr-2609242330). amu's own source manipulates EDN data of arbitrary
  ;; shape (HIR, KIR, ns forms), so compiling amu with amu needs that data
  ;; model on every target, native included. Measured as the selfhost walls
  ;; of 2026-09-24/26 (per-file project check, grant
  ;; lang/selfhost-compiler-grant.edn). Appended after the browser floors so
  ;; the loop reaches them last; each closes like any other floor, by its
  ;; gate on origin/main, and a floor taken by another writer is left to it.
  {:id :document-type-predicates :gate "document-type-predicates-ask-the-kind-test"
   :goal "map? vector? set? list? seq? coll? keyword? string? symbol? integer? boolean? true? false? nil? some? on a :document are its run-time document-kind; on a static type the type's answer; on [:option T] presence when T answers true; an option whose payload answers by value, nil? on a type with no absence and map? on a [:ref q] stay refused by name"
   :amends "kotoba-lang guest-grammar :true? / :integer? (a :document was refused by name)"}
  {:id :expression-absence :gate "expression-absence-typed-by-the-present-branch-test"
   :goal "a missing else (when, when-not, if-not, when-let, if-let, cond) and a literal nil branch answer nothing, typed by the present branch: false beside :bool, the option's none beside an option, [:option T] beside any other T (an :i64 too where the result is inferred), the legacy 0 where the author declared :i64; a loop's exits join the same way; an absent i64 used as a number, two present types and an else-less if stay refused by name"
   :amends "kotoba-lang guest-grammar :when (the i64 0 as the absent value); ADR 0353 point 2 (nil as a map-literal value) carried to expression level"}
  {:id :native-abort :gate "native-abort-compiles-verifies-and-packages-test"
   :goal "throw / try (the abort ability, lowered to [:result T E] values) compile for aarch64-macos and x86_64, the verifier admits :abort beside :state and re-derives the sealed answer, and the linux-static packager needs no handler for it; an ex-info (:document) error stays refused on native by name until :native-document"
   :amends "kotoba-lang lang/abort-ability.edn :backends (native :not-qualified)"}
  {:id :native-document :gate "native-document-values-test"
   :goal "a :document on aarch64-macos and x86_64: the canonical EDN text in the string handle native documents already were; construction, get / assoc / dissoc / merge, count, kind, the vector / list / set / map-entry accessors, sort, the scalar accessors and structural equality lowered onto the string slots plus emitted helpers, answering what the reference and restricted ESM answer; ex-info on native; f64 documents, the sha256 digest and the hex codec stay refused by name"
   :amends "kotoba-lang surface-status :contextual-document-literal (native had no document operations)"}]}
